[{"answer":"The person I've chosen to talk about is the French writer Victor Hugo -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/1.mp3"},{"answer":"many people have heard of him because his novel, Les Miserables,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/2.mp3"},{"answer":"which he wrote in 1862, is famous around the world.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/3.mp3"},{"answer":"It became a stage musical in the 1980s,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/4.mp3"},{"answer":"and a film version was also released in 2012.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/5.mp3"},{"answer":"So, some of us, I'm sure, have a pretty general idea of the plot,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/6.mp3"},{"answer":"but we know much less about the author.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/7.mp3"},{"answer":"Today, I'm going to provide a little more insight into this talented man","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/8.mp3"},{"answer":"and I'm going to talk particularly about the home he had on the island of Guernsey in the British Channel Islands.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/9.mp3"},{"answer":"But first, his early career...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/10.mp3"},{"answer":"as I've said, he was a writer,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/11.mp3"},{"answer":"he was at the height of his career in Paris","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/12.mp3"},{"answer":"and he was very highly regarded by his colleagues.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/13.mp3"},{"answer":"As far as literature was concerned,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/14.mp3"},{"answer":"he was the leading figure of the Romantic movement.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/15.mp3"},{"answer":"However, as well as being a literary genius,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/16.mp3"},{"answer":"he also gave many speeches about issues like the level of poverty in his society.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/17.mp3"},{"answer":"He felt very strongly about this","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/18.mp3"},{"answer":"and about other areas where change was needed, like education.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/19.mp3"},{"answer":"This kind of outspoken criticism was not well liked by the rulers of France","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/20.mp3"},{"answer":"and, eventually, the emperor - Napoleon III -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/21.mp3"},{"answer":"told Victor Hugo to leave Paris and not return;","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/22.mp3"},{"answer":"in other words, he sent him into exile.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/23.mp3"},{"answer":"So Victor Hugo was forced to reside in other parts of Europe.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/24.mp3"},{"answer":"Guernsey was actually his third place of exile","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/25.mp3"},{"answer":"and he landed there in 1855.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/26.mp3"},{"answer":"He produced a lot while on Guernsey - including Les Miserables -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/27.mp3"},{"answer":"and to do this, he had to spend a great deal of time in the home that he had there.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/28.mp3"},{"answer":"This was a property that he bought using the money he'd made in France","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/29.mp3"},{"answer":"from the publication of a collection of his poetry.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/30.mp3"},{"answer":"It was the only property he ever owned, and he was very proud of it.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/31.mp3"},{"answer":"The property Victor Hugo bought on Guernsey was a large, five-storey house in the capital town of St Peter Port","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/32.mp3"},{"answer":"and he lived there for 15 years,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/33.mp3"},{"answer":"returning to France in 1870 when Napoleon's Empire collapsed.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/34.mp3"},{"answer":"He decorated and furnished each level, or floor, of the house in unique and wonderful ways,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/35.mp3"},{"answer":"and many people consider the inside of the house to be a 'work of art'.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/36.mp3"},{"answer":"Today it's a museum that attracts 200,000 visitors a year.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/37.mp3"},{"answer":"He lived in the house with his family...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/38.mp3"},{"answer":"and portraits of its members still hang in rooms on the ground floor,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/39.mp3"},{"answer":"along with drawings that he did during his travels that he felt were important to him.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/40.mp3"},{"answer":"In other ground-floor rooms, there are huge tapestries","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/41.mp3"},{"answer":"that he would've designed and loved.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/42.mp3"},{"answer":"The walls are covered in dark wood panelling that Victor Hugo created himself","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/43.mp3"},{"answer":"using wooden furniture that he bought in the market.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/44.mp3"},{"answer":"The items were relatively inexpensive,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/45.mp3"},{"answer":"and he used them to create intricate carvings.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/46.mp3"},{"answer":"They gave an atmosphere on the lower level that was shadowy and rather solemn.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/47.mp3"},{"answer":"On the next level of the house there are two impressive lounges,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/48.mp3"},{"answer":"where he entertained his guests.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/49.mp3"},{"answer":"One lounge has entirely red furnishings,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/50.mp3"},{"answer":"such as sofas and wall coverings, and the other blue.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/51.mp3"},{"answer":"There's a strong Chinese influence in these areas","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/52.mp3"},{"answer":"in things like the wallpaper pattern and the lamps -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/53.mp3"},{"answer":"which he would have made himself by copying original versions.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/54.mp3"},{"answer":"His library, where he left many of his favourite books,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/55.mp3"},{"answer":"forms the hallway to the third floor","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/56.mp3"},{"answer":"and was a comfortable area where he could relax and enjoy his afternoons.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/57.mp3"},{"answer":"And then, at the very top of the house,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/58.mp3"},{"answer":"there's a room called the Lookout -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/59.mp3"},{"answer":"called that because it looks out over the harbour.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/60.mp3"},{"answer":"In contrast to the rather dark lower levels,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/61.mp3"},{"answer":"it's full of light and was like a glass office where he would write until lunchtime -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/62.mp3"},{"answer":"often at his desk.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/63.mp3"},{"answer":"So, Victor Hugo was a man of many talents,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/64.mp3"},{"answer":"but he was also true to his values.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/65.mp3"},{"answer":"While living in his house on Guernsey,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/66.mp3"},{"answer":"he entertained many other famous writers,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/67.mp3"},{"answer":"but he also invited a large group of local children from the deprived areas of the island to dinner once a week.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/68.mp3"},{"answer":"What's more, he served them their food,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/69.mp3"},{"answer":"which was an extraordinary gesture for the time period.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/70.mp3"},{"answer":"In 1927, the house was owned by his relatives,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/71.mp3"},{"answer":"and they decided to donate it to the city of Paris.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/72.mp3"},{"answer":"It has since been restored using photographs from the period","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/73.mp3"},{"answer":"and, as I mentioned earlier, is now a museum that is open to the public.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-4-part-4-2023-06-17-19-17-54/74.mp3"}]
